DisplayStrings = (
" ",
A,
ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ,
WAVE,
"Pack my box with five dozen liquor jugs.
Type is a beautiful group of letters, not a group of beautiful letters.
ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ  abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz  0123456789
Kerning fixes the space between two letters; tracking spreads them all.
Legibility is the foundation of a quiet, generous page.
Simplicity is the ultimate sophistication.
A well-made typeface reads without being noticed.
Waltz, bad nymph, for quick jigs vex.
The book runs 320 pages, priced at $24.99, released on May 3rd.
Jackdaws love my big sphinx of quartz.

A specimen shows a typeface at work. Set in running paragraphs, the letters find their rhythm; the spacing between words settles, and the texture of the page slowly reveals the designer's hand.

Reading is a fragile act of trust. The eye moves along a line, expecting each shape to behave, and a good typeface never breaks that promise. It carries the voice of the writer without raising its own.",
"쀍쁑뿕 뜕낢괞 쉪뚧뷁 쐥쓩믜 뺘뺖뷗 뷖뜢쒝 꿹꼵쓙 뙗뙉듥 뽥뾱쫍 쫥뺡쁑.

꽓꽔뷖 뷗뺖뺘 쓜쓩쐥 뷁뚧쉪 괞낢믜 뜕뿕쁑 쀍쒝쓙 꼵꿹뜢 뜿뷖뷗.

뜢뜿뷖 뷗뺖뺘 쓜쓩쐥 뷁뚧쉪 괞낢믜 뜕뿕쁑 쀍쒝쓙 꼵꿹뜢 꽓꽔뷗.

뙉뙗꽓 꽔괞낢 믜쓩쐥 뷁뚧쉪 뜕뿕쁑 쀍쒝쓙 꼵꿹뜢 뜿뷖뷗 뺖뺘쓜.

뺖뺘쓜 쓩뙉뙗 꽓꽔괞 낢믜쓩 쐥뜕뿕 쁑쀍쒝 쓙꼵꿹 뜢뜿뷖 뷗뺡뾱."
